core_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":-2.0520801730749167,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":0.0,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.005203128934520973,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":55.2,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":-0.030973602726778977,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":0.0,"_gate_share_shrink":0.1305706111463938,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.2518209236786863,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0051700003,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":3.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Insmed Incorporated develops and commercializes therapies for patients with serious and rare diseases in the United States, Europe, Japan, and internationally. The company offers ARIKAYCE for the treatment of refractory nontuberculous mycobacterial lung infections, as well as is in phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of mycobacterium avium complex lung disease as part of a combination antibacterial drug regimen for adult patients. It also develops brensocatib, an oral reversible inhibitor of dipeptidyl peptidase 1(DPP1) that is in phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of bronchiectasis; and in phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of chronic rhinosinusitis without nasal polyps and hidradenitis suppurativa. In addition, the company is developing treprostinil palmitil inhalation powder, an inhaled formulation of a treprostinil prodrug treprostinil palmitil, which is in phase 3 clinical trial for the treatment of pulmonary hypertension associated with interstitial lung disease; and phase 2 clinical trial for the treatment of pulmonary arterial hypertension. Further, it develops INS1201, a microdystrophin adeno-associated virus gene replacement therapy which is in phase 1 clinical trial for the treatment of Duchenne muscular dystrophy, as well as it is also developing pre-clinical research programs for gene therapy, AI-driven protein engineering, protein manufacturing, RNA end-joining, and synthetic rescue. In addition, it provides INS1148, monoclonal antibody targeting stem cell factor called SCF248 that is in phase-2 clinical trial for the treatment of interstitial lung disease, and asthma; and INS1202, an intrathecally delivered gene therapy which is in phase 1 of clinical trial for the treatment of amyotrophic lateral sclerosis. The company was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in Bridgewater, New Jersey.","ceo_bio":"Mr. William H. Lewis J.D., M.B.A. | President, CEO & Chairman | Age 56 | Compensation: $2.5M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Healthcare peers, with revenue growing 42%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $92K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 7\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Insmed Incorporated is a large-cap healthcare business with a $26.6B market cap on $606M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +35% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -281% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 82% confirm genuine pricing power.","The company is burning through $968M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -14.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 3.1% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 205% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $46.4M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Patent cliffs, drug-pricing reform, and reimbursement pressure \u2014 a single regulatory change can reset the pricing power that justifies the multiple.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Clinical trial concentration risk \u2014 binary FDA outcomes on a lead asset can wipe out billions in market cap in a single session.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"GLP-1 disruption across sub-sectors \u2014 weight-loss drugs are reshaping demand for orthopaedics, cardiovascular devices, and sleep-apnea treatments in ways not yet priced in.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Valued at a 369% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Healthcare peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Healthcare sector showing strong relative momentum, outperforming the market by 13% over 3 months","Healthcare ETF in a sustained uptrend above its long-term average","Strong 6-month sector performance (30.7% return)"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Fulcrum Asset Management LLP Acquires New Holdings in Insmed, Inc. $INSM","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/fulcrum-asset-management-llp-acquires-new-holdings-in-insmed-inc-insm.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794475883.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.944,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["m_and_a"]},{"title":"(INSM) Movement Within Algorithmic Entry Frameworks","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/INSM_Movement_Within_Algorithmic_Entry_Frameworks_111226123002_1794461402.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794461402.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Insmed (INSM) Raises 2026 Guidance Following Earnings, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/pharmaceuticals-biotech/nasdaq-insm/insmed/news/insmed-insm-raises-2026-guidance-following-earnings-is-it-st","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794093549.54,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.735,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","guidance"]},{"title":"Insmed (NASDAQ:INSM) vs. Moderna (NASDAQ:MRNA) Financial Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/07/insmed-nasdaqinsm-vs-moderna-nasdaqmrna-financial-survey.html","date":"2026-11-07","timestamp":1794064231.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.935,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"17,585 Insmed, Inc. $INSM Shares Purchased by Sumitomo Mitsui Trust Group Inc.","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincol